# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: entity-access-arx-vba-vendor-divergences -- ENTMAKE / ENTMOD / SSGET ERRNO, ENTGET order, ARX ONFAILURE and VBA, as AutoCAD / BricsCAD do
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: divergence
#+DEPENDS: windows-runner-sunset-probe-campaign
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-11-16

Measured by the sunset campaign's B7 (probe-arx-vba.lsp) and B9
(probe-entity-access.lsp). Captured 2026-11-16 by !551's probe:suite jobs: AutoCAD 2022 Windows (job
18080296904, probe-results/autocad/ms-windows/20261116T191007Z), BricsCAD
Windows (18080296908, .../bricscad/ms-windows/20261116T191739Z), BricsCAD
macOS (18080296905, .../bricscad/macos/20261116T190931Z). Each cell is
(RESULT ERRNO-AFTER).
clautolisp's own run of the same suites (2026-11-16, before the capture) is
the baseline the points below compare against.

* Divergences to model

1. =(entmake '((0 . "NOSUCHTYPE")))= returns its data list in clautolisp;
   nil on all three products (AutoCAD ERRNO 36, BricsCAD 0). NOT a plain bug:
   VALIDATE-ENTITY-DXF (drawing/entity-families.lisp) accepts an
   unregistered type on purpose -- clautolisp cannot enumerate every DXF
   entity the vendor knows, and a valid client entity it has no descriptor
   for must not be refused. Rejecting unknown types as the products do needs
   pjb's decision (and probably the vendors' full entity-type list).
2. ERRNO of failing entity calls: AutoCAD sets it -- ENTMAKE of an unknown
   type 36, of a LINE without points 47, without a type 30; ENTMOD without
   (-1 . ename) 47; ENTNEXT past the end 8; SSGET "X" with a malformed -4
   list 56-61 -- where BricsCAD leaves 0. clautolisp leaves 0 for the
   ENTMAKE / SSGET cases, but SIGNALS for ENTMOD without (-1 . ename) and for
   (entmod nil), where both products return nil; and it leaves ERRNO 4 after
   (entget nil) / (entupd nil), where both products signal with ERRNO 0.
   Per product.
3. ENTGET's leading order: AutoCAD (-1 0 330 5 ...), BricsCAD (-1 0 5 330
   ...); clautolisp gives AutoCAD's. Per product.
4. ENTMOD of an XRECORD in the named-object dictionary: AutoCAD returns T
   but does NOT apply the change; BricsCAD applies it; clautolisp returned
   nil and did not apply it.
5. ARXLOAD / ARXUNLOAD of a missing module: AutoCAD signals unless ONFAILURE
   is given, then returns ONFAILURE (ERRNO 93 / 94); BricsCAD signals even
   with ONFAILURE; clautolisp returns nil. The (arx) list is the product's.
6. VL-VBALOAD of a missing project: AutoCAD batch signals (no VBA object in
   accoreconsole), BricsCAD returns nil; VL-VBARUN of a missing macro:
   AutoCAD T, BricsCAD nil (Windows ERRNO 101). clautolisp nil / nil.

Agreed by all three (nothing to change): ENTDEL twice returns T both times;
an ownerless XRECORD never becomes ENTLAST and an ENTNEXT walk meets only
graphical entities; ENTGET / ENTUPD of nil signal a bad argument; malformed
SSGET "X" filters return nil.

