* Progress -- 2026-11-16 (clautolisp 2.4.22)

- [X] 1. ENTMAKE / ENTMAKEX refuse a type nobody knows (pjb: do like the
  products): VALIDATE-ENTITY-DXF refuses a type that is neither a family nor
  in *KNOWN-DXF-TYPES* (the DXF reference's ENTITIES / OBJECTS sections,
  tables, records, BLOCK / ENDBLK); a known type without a family (WIPEOUT)
  is still taken unchanged.
- [X] 2. ERRNO of failing entity calls, per product (AutoCAD; BricsCAD 0):
  ENTMAKE without a type 30, unknown type 36, missing group 47 (the host
  reports the reason in *ENTMAKE-FAILURE-REASON*); ENTMOD without
  (-1 . ename) returns nil with 47 instead of signalling, (entmod nil) nil
  with 0; ENTNEXT past the end 8; a bad ename (ENTGET / ENTUPD of nil)
  leaves 0. And VL-CATCH-ALL-APPLY no longer resets ERRNO after a successful
  call -- AutoCAD's codes survive it. And SSGET with a malformed -4
  grouping: nil on both, AutoCAD ERRNO 56 (left open) / 58 (unknown
  operator) / 59 (closer without opener) / 61 (NOT without one operand),
  BricsCAD 0 (2.4.23, %SSGET-FILTER-ERRNO).
- [X] 3. ENTGET order per product: already modelled (%VENDOR-HEADER-ORDER,
  from entget-pointers section 10); B9 confirms it on all three.
- [X] 4. ENTMOD of a dictionary XRECORD: the AutoCAD no-op (D3) now returns
  the data, as AutoCAD answered non-nil; BricsCAD applies, as before (2.4.23).
- [ ] 5. ARXLOAD / ARXUNLOAD ONFAILURE.
- [ ] 6. VL-VBALOAD / VL-VBARUN.

